  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam Internal Audit Capacity Building for Ministry of Finance Inspectorate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project will aim to build the capacity of Internal Audit for Inspectorate of Vietnam Ministry of Finance, specifically this project will develop the Manual of Internal Auditing Procedures and the Risk Assessment Framework for Inspectorate of Ministry of Finance of Vietnam.  It is noted that this is the updated proposal for Internal Audit Capacity Strenthening. The initial proposal (P120491) was dropped since the proposed activities could not be conducted in the timeframe of the project. The development objective of the grant is to build capacity for Inspectorate of Ministry of Finance (MOF) in Internal Audit through effectively implementing of internal auditing within the MOF and leading internal auditing across the public sector. The grant is expected to contribute to the enhancement of quality and effectiveness of the internal control system in the Public Financial Management (PFM) leading to a more efficient and effective management, control and use of public resources and reduced fraud, waste and abuse of public resources.</narrative>
  </description>
